 bombing against Japan, but also proved very good for night incendiary bombing at low altitude. The aircraft was also used to drop the atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The B-29 was one of the largest aircraft built during WWII and its design included very advanced technology for its time, such as a pressurized cabin and an analog computer controlled firing system that allowed crew members to remotely control four machine gun turrets. 3,970 B-29s were built and the aircraft stayed in use until 1960.","LocalizedString":"The Boeing B-29 Superfortress was an American heavy bomber used in WWII by the US Army Air Force, the US Air Force and the Royal Air Force. The B-29 was primarily used for high-altitude strategic bombing against Japan, but also proved very good for night incendiary bombing at low altitude. The aircraft was also used to drop the atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The B-29 was one of the largest aircraft built during WWII and its design included very advanced technology for its time, such as a pressurized cabin and an analog computer controlled firing system that allowed crew members to remotely control four machine gun turrets. 3,970 B-29s were built and the aircraft stayed in use until 1960."},"operationCost":4,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Blitz","EHelpBubbleTypes::HeavyArmor2"],"hasDeployment":true,"hasBlitz":true,"heavyArmor":2,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'au_aircraft_large'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/au_aircraft_large.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_b-29_superfortress.t_b-29_superfortress","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Robert Taylor","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/B-29_SUPER_FORTRESS.B-29_SUPER_FORTRESS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":394.0},"historyPhotoSource":"United States Air Force Historical Re